.TH RANMA-DUMP-LAYOUT 1 "" "ranma 0.3.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-dump\-layout \- Print a layout as the \fBranma.layout(...)\fR call that declares it, to paste into init.lua: the workspace this runs in, or NAME (declared or saved): \fBranma dump\-layout >> ~/.config/ranma/lua/layouts.lua\fR
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma dump\-layout\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a layout as the \fBranma.layout(...)\fR call that declares it, to paste into init.lua: the workspace this runs in, or NAME (declared or saved): \fBranma dump\-layout >> ~/.config/ranma/lua/layouts.lua\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
A layout \fBload_layout\fR takes; the shown workspace when left out
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
